  "notes": "Source: Carrington College Respiratory Therapy Program Handbook (©2025), 'Program Progression' table: 'Course progression through the RT program is as shown below. Students must complete courses sequentially; failing a core course or on-ground general education course or taking a leave of absence will necessitate a retake of that course, impeding progression to the next term.' Terms are 15 weeks with a 1-week break between terms; general-education courses are online, RCS/RCP courses on ground (RCP210/220/230 are clinical/extern). Total 86 units = 18+16+17+18+17. Course codes kept verbatim as printed in the handbook, including inconsistent spacing (\"MTH 151\", \"ENG 101\", \"RCP 220\", \"RCP 180\", \"RCP 190\", \"RCP 230\" printed with a space; \"RCS115\", \"RCP100\", etc. without). Titles taken from the Carrington College Academic Catalog Volume XI.III (effective April 12, 2025–December 31, 2026) course descriptions. Genuine catalog conflict documented: the May 2026 Supplement to Catalog Volume XII (revision date March 28, 2026) lists RCP160 as 4 units (45/45 hours) and RCP170 as 6 units (60/60 hours), while both the main catalog (updated October 24, 2025) and the RT Program Handbook list RCP160 as 3 units (60 total hours) and RCP170 as 7 units (150 total hours); both versions sum to 86 units and keep Term 4 at 18 units — the handbook values (source of the term layout) are seeded verbatim. Title variant in catalog: the RT program course list prints \"RCP100 Introduction of Respiratory Care\" while the course-description heading prints \"RCP100 Introduction to Respiratory Care\" (seeded with the description title); RCS135 appears as \"Microbiology For The Respiratory Care Therapist With Lab\" in the RT course list vs \"Microbiology\" in the description heading. GOV141 (American Government, required for Nevada students only) excluded: the Phoenix campus is in Arizona, where HUM200 (Ethics in Contemporary Society) is the general-education course. Program is offered at the Phoenix campus (catalog program page lists Phoenix among offering campuses); not offered at Mesa. Phoenix campus relocating effective November 2025 to 2421 W. Peoria Ave Ste 130/200, Phoenix AZ 85029.",
